As an identity of formal power series over $\mathbb Q$,
\begin{equation}
\sum_{n\ge1}a_nx^n=
\frac{8x(17-7488x+974848x^2-40108032x^3)}
{(1-64x)(1-1600x+368640x^2-21233664x^3)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for $n\ge5$,
\begin{equation}
a_n=1664a_{n-1}-471040a_{n-2}+44826624a_{n-3}-1358954496a_{n-4},
\end{equation}
with $a_1=136$, $a_2=166400$, $a_3=220626944$, and $a_4=294517735424$.

The number $A(G)$ of these normalized colorings is
\begin{equation}
A(G)=\frac{2^N}{48}\bigl(P_G(3)+3P_G(2)+15P_G(1)\bigr).
\end{equation}
If $G$ is connected and bipartite with at least one edge, this becomes
$A(G)=2^N(P_G(3)+6)/48$.

All empirical row recurrences in the FORMULA block of A233256, revision 6,
hold on their stated ranges. In particular, Barker's formulas in A233257,
revision 8 \cite{rowtwo}, and A233258, revision 8 \cite{rowthree},
and Hardin's recurrence in A233259, revision 6 \cite{rowfour}, hold:
\begin{align*}
F_2(x)&=\frac{x(3-38x+88x^2)}{(1-4x)(1-12x)},\\
F_3(x)&=\frac{x(11-392x+3072x^2-8192x^3+16384x^4)}
{(1-8x)(1-40x+128x^2)},\\
a_{4,w}&=160a_{4,w-1}-6144a_{4,w-2}+86016a_{4,w-3}
-393216a_{4,w-4}\quad(w\ge9).
\end{align*}
Also $a_{2,w}=2^{2w-3}(4\cdot3^w+9)/9$ for $w>1$.
